WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.240
Pollsters have been asking about impeaching
President Trump for some time.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.500
In the latest Harvard/HarrisX poll, 42 percent
said that he should be impeached and removed from

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.740
office for his actions, while 41 percent said
no action should be taken.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.680
There have been only a few ripples in this
trend since Harvard/Harris first asked the

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.490
question in June 2017.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.860
Another question with a different emphasis
asked by Quinnipiac University since January

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.600
this year provides a different perspective.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:39.310
In August 2018, 58 percent of registered voters
said that they would not like to see the Democratic

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.340
Party begin impeachment proceedings if the Democrats

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.400
regain control of the House of Representatives in November.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:48.629
Thirty-six percent said that they should proceed.

00:00:48.629 --> 00:00:55.030
A majority of voters in the June 2018 NBC News/Wall
Street Journal poll said that their vote in November

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.149
would not be a signal either way on impeachment.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:03.550
Twenty-two percent said it would send a signal
to impeach Trump, while a similar 25 percent

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.120
said it would send a signal in opposition
to impeachment.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.520
This is a sensitive issue with serious political ramifications. Let us know what you think,

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.240
let us know your comments.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.240
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.380
and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

